            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The sine and cosine rules give ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\sin A=\\dfrac{a\\sin C}{c}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\cos A=\\dfrac{b-a\\cos C}{c}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". Divide and simplify.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "By the sine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin A&=\\frac{a\\sin C}{c}.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos A&=\\frac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2bc},\\\\c^2&=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute the expression for $c^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos A&=\\frac{b^2+(a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C)-a^2}{2bc}\\\\\\cos A&=\\frac{b-a\\cos C}{c}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $A\\ne90^\\circ$, $\\cos A\\ne0$. Divide $\\sin A$ by $\\cos A$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan A&=\\frac{a\\sin C/c}{(b-a\\cos C)/c}\\\\\\tan A&=\\frac{a\\sin C}{b-a\\cos C}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
